desc:Haruki - ten-lane drum instrument
tags: instrument sampler drums sequencer
author: Michele Ibba
version: 2.1
about:
  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
  Haruki is a ten-channel sample player with a host-synchronised step sequencer.
  Drag a WAV onto a channel to load it. Each step carries velocity, probability,
  substeps and microtiming.

  Outputs 1-2 always carry the mix of all ten channels. Outputs 3-12 carry the
  ten channels one by one, in order, mono and ahead of the pan control.

  LICENSE: GPL v2 or later.
  This plug-in embeds the ladder filter from REAPER's stock JSFX "Moog 4-Pole
  Filter" (Effects/Liteon/moog24db), (C) 2008-2009 Lubomir I. Ivanov, released
  under the GPL; that filter in turn implements the Moog approximation from the
  Stilson/Smith CCRMA paper by way of the CSound source. Because that code is
  included here, Haruki as a whole is distributed under the GPL.
  Ivanov's notice is reproduced in full, unaltered, beside the filter itself;
  it asks to be acknowledged, and this is that acknowledgement.
  See <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.

in_pin:none
out_pin:Left
out_pin:Right
out_pin:Ch1 Out
out_pin:Ch2 Out
out_pin:Ch3 Out
out_pin:Ch4 Out
out_pin:Ch5 Out
out_pin:Ch6 Out
out_pin:Ch7 Out
out_pin:Ch8 Out
out_pin:Ch9 Out
out_pin:Ch10 Out

options:maxmem=17000000 no_meter gfx_hz=30

// ---- per channel: 9 parameters each, sliders 1..90 (all hidden, the UI is @gfx)
slider1:0<-60,12,0.1>-Ch1 Gain (dB)
slider2:0<-100,100,1>-Ch1 Pan
slider3:0<-24,24,0.01>-Ch1 Tune (semitones)
slider4:0<0,100,0.01>-Ch1 Start
slider5:0<0,100,0.1>-Ch1 Attack
slider6:0<0,100,0.1>-Ch1 Decay
slider7:100<0,100,0.1>-Ch1 Cutoff
slider8:0<0,100,0.1>-Ch1 Resonance
slider9:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Ch1 Mute
slider10:0<-60,12,0.1>-Ch2 Gain (dB)
slider11:0<-100,100,1>-Ch2 Pan
slider12:0<-24,24,0.01>-Ch2 Tune (semitones)
slider13:0<0,100,0.01>-Ch2 Start
slider14:0<0,100,0.1>-Ch2 Attack
